    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **James Wood** headlining our lineup at an elite 76.28 score. Facing a favorable matchup against Lorenzen (4.82 xERA), **James Wood** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+14%) and an elite xwOBA profile that positions him as our top target for high-ceiling production. We also see strong value in **Vinnie Pasquantino** (69.99), who draws a significant +14% platoon advantage against Mahle, and **Isaac Paredes** (68.21), whose matchup against Phillips presents an ideal intersection of SP skill decay and prime lineup placement. **Corbin Carroll** remains a staple of our strategy; despite facing a tougher arm in Perkins (3.52 xERA), his high base projection and favorable order placement secure a 64.96 score, keeping him in the high-leverage tier we prioritize for our 5x5 objectives.\n\nThe decision to bench **Josh Naylor** (52.67) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Josh Naylor** produced a respectable efficiency score, the combination of a tough matchup against Burns (3.59 xERA) and negative park factors ultimately pushed him behind the production threshold of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Max Muncy**. We are keeping a close eye on **Seiya Suzuki** (62.95); while he provides a solid floor, the 42% rain risk and inward-blowing wind represent significant volatility that could dampen his output. Elsewhere, **Mickey Moniak** is deployed primarily for the park factor boost (+14%), though we are cognizant that his low order spot and platoon disadvantage keep his ceiling moderate. We are also monitoring the status of **Jose Caballero**, who remains sidelined today due to a postponement; his absence necessitates that our active roster players\u2014including **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Brice Turang**\u2014maintain their current efficiency levels to offset the loss of potential stolen base volume.",
